<p>they dont need to be supernatural, but this isnt quite even into the realm of the "abnormal". it doesnt exist, but this would be a legitimate evolutionary strategy i could see a species of insect developing.</p>
<p>classifying them as an SCP doesnt make much sense, there's nothing about them that needs to be "contained" inherently. this would be like classifying any dangerous species as an SCP. if the public was aware of these they'd have to be cautious in case they had them, but it'd just mean pesticides.</p>
<p>i like the idea of this one and your writing on the article is good. it's scary in concept, and the idea of it possibly being real does make it just that much worse. but i do think it needs something more to push it into SCP territory. not voting yet.</p>
